Subject: [PATCH 2/2] es: record WHY each object escapes, in a side map

WHAT THIS CHANGES
-----------------
Adds two files and edits eight, ~330 lines net:

  es/EscapeReason.java    new. One enum constant per site in the analysis that can put
                          Escape into a status, with isSurrender() splitting "the program
                          does this" from "the analysis gave up".
  es/EscapeReasons.java   new. A static, append-only side map
                          Map<SootMethod, Map<ObjectNode, EnumSet<EscapeReason>>>.
  ptg/PointsToGraph       gains `public SootMethod method` and an EscapeReason argument on
                          cascadeEscape/recursiveCascadeEscape.
  handlers/*              each Escape-introducing site stamps its own constant.
  analyser/StaticAnalyser sets ptg.method in apply(); stamps NO_BCI_METHOD.
  utils/KillCallerOnly    stamps CALLER_ONLY_UNRESOLVABLE.
  resolver/ReworkedResolver  adds collectReasons(), a non-short-circuiting twin of
                          resolve() that writes only to the side map.
  main/Main               exposes MarkStoreEscaping as argv[7]; writes <dirname>.reasons.

WHY
---
Escape multiplicity cannot be recovered from the lattice after the fact. `Escape` is a
singleton with hashCode() == 0 (es/Escape.java) and EscapeStatus.purge() /
purgeAndEscape() replace the whole status set with {Escape} the moment escape is
established. So today every escaping object has exactly one status and every NoEscape
object has none, and a "number of escape reasons" plot has two bars by construction.
The reasons have to be captured at the moment they fire, in a structure the lattice does
not own. That is what the side map is.

THE ESCAPE VERDICT MUST NOT CHANGE, AND THAT IS CHECKABLE
---------------------------------------------------------
Nothing in the analysis ever reads the side map. Three specific design choices exist so
that this claim is verifiable rather than asserted:

  * resolve() is NOT modified. The four conditions are re-evaluated by a separate
    collectReasons() which never calls SetComponent and never writes solvedSummaries.
  * collectReasons() runs immediately BEFORE resolve() for each component, inside FindSCC,
    not after FindSCC returns. FindSCC *is* the resolution loop: resolve() mutates
    solvedSummaries per component in reverse topological order and a later component's
    successor test reads what earlier ones wrote. Evaluating after the loop would test a
    different state and would report TRANSITIVE_SUCCESSOR for nearly everything. This is a
    deliberate deviation from the design note, made for fidelity, and it does not weaken
    the diff check.
  * collectReasons() stamps the WHOLE component, mirroring SetComponent. resolve() escapes
    every member when any one member fires, so attributing the reason only to the firing
    member leaves the others Escape with an empty reason set. Measured on corpus/M02 before
    this was changed: 3 of 7 objects, whose component's reason had fired on a callee
    parameter node in another method.
  * cascadeEscape's reason argument is required rather than defaulted, so a new call site
    cannot silently produce an unattributed escape: the compiler names every one.

The check is: run every stava/tests/* under the uninstrumented and the instrumented build
and diff <dirname>.res. See Micro-Corpus-Log Phase 11, F11.1.

argv[7]
-------
Main.setStoreEscapeOptions already read argv[5] (ReduceParamDependence) and argv[6]
(MarkParamReturnEscaping). MarkStoreEscaping, the largest precision lever in the codebase,
was reachable only by editing config/StoreEscape.java and recompiling — which is the only
reason patches/0001-store-escape-off.patch exists. It is now argv[7]. The compiled-in
default is unchanged: config/StoreEscape.java still ships MarkStoreEscaping = true.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE
-----------------------
No lattice type, no handler control flow, no resolver decision, no .info format, no .res
format, no stats.txt. One new output file, <dirname>.reasons, written once and truncating,
sorted, joinable on (method signature, bci, objectType).

HOW IT IS APPLIED
-----------------
NEVER to stava/. build.sh copies stava/src to heapviz/build/stava-src-reason/ and applies
this patch to the copy. It is independent of 0001: with argv[7] available, the pye
configuration no longer needs a patched source tree, and 0001 is retained only to reproduce
phases 1-10 (USE_PATCH=1).

